On 2007-12-05, Cuboidz <Dieter.Bercx@gmail.com> wrote:
> So I'm wondering whether it is feasible to just use shops for shopping
> only? And in the same vein: what do you (usually) do when you
> encounter a shop?

It's quite feasible and you really don't give up _that_ much... mostly
because it's unlikely to find _that_ many shops outside of Minetown, so a game 
in which you don't price-ID stuff in a bookstore looks much like a game 
in which you didn't find a bookstore in the first place.  Given that the latter 
is perfectly workable, the former is as well; the price-ID stuff is a
tradeoff of the player's time for extra information.

I normally only bother to price-ID the scroll of identify unless I simply 
don't have very many scrolls of identify to begin with; then i'll 
occasionally go hunting for the under-100 scrolls as well.  I keep in 
mind what the prices are likely to be for things on the floor in case I 
see some boots I might want to buy or a nice, really really expensive wand, 
but soon enough the shopkeepers can't stand up to you anymore, so 
bash-n-grab is perfectly viable as a solution.

And after a different point, you're walking around with enough gold to
buy anything you want at any time you want, so you don't even need to
bash-n-grab.

